      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَزْوَى</span></b> , (K,) said of a man, (TA,) [from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَوٌّ</span>,]
<i>He came having with him another:</i> (K, and T
in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تو</span>:) mentioned by Az and Sgh on the
authority of IAar: (TA:) opposed to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَتْوَى</span> meaning “ he came alone; by himself. ” (T in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تو</span>.)

